# gstack in Cursor

gstack is a specialist workflow suite. Skills live in `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`. When a request matches a skill, **Read that file and follow it** before answering. Do not improvise a thinner version.

## Sprint order

Think → Plan → Build → Review → Test → Ship → Reflect

- New product idea / "is this worth building" → `/office-hours`
- Strategy / scope / ambition → `/plan-ceo-review`
- Architecture / data flow / tests → `/plan-eng-review`
- Visual design of a plan → `/plan-design-review`
- DX of a plan (CLI/API/SDK) → `/plan-devex-review`
- Run the full review gauntlet → `/autoplan`
- Vague intent → GitHub issue → `/spec`
- Bug / error / "why is this broken" → `/investigate`
- Code review / diff → `/review`
- Test a live site and fix → `/qa` (report only: `/qa-only`)
- Ready to push / PR → `/ship`
- Security audit → `/cso`

## Cursor tools (never Claude Code names)

Use `AskQuestion`, `Shell`, `Task`, `StrReplace`, `Read`, `Grep`, `Glob`. Read `AGENTS.md` for project conventions, not `CLAUDE.md`. Browser work uses the gstack browse binary (`browse/dist/browse` or `bun run dev`), never Chrome MCP tools.

## Project config

Read `AGENTS.md` first. Persist durable project answers there so they are not re-asked.
